1
00:00:00,780 --> 00:00:04,400
Imagine bringing a new idea into a team of people and

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,900
agents, and building on what everyone else has already made.

3
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:13,060
Constellation gives that collaboration five useful building blocks.

4
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,860
An experience is where people interact.

5
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:19,960
A conversation brings participants and history together.

6
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,640
A connection lets an agent participate.

7
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,880
The Agent Instance provides a continuing

8
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,960
identity and a dependable boundary.

9
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,840
Tools supply useful capabilities.

10
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,080
Conversations and tools can be shared across many agents.

11
00:00:37,947 --> 00:00:41,027
Inside that agent, there is room to invent.

12
00:00:41,907 --> 00:00:44,507
You might choose one engine, such as Constellation

13
00:00:44,507 --> 00:00:49,067
Runtime, Codex, Claude, Copilot or Amplifier Agent.

14
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:54,207
You might assemble an inner team that explores, builds and reviews.

15
00:00:55,027 --> 00:00:56,927
Or design a different arrangement around

16
00:00:56,927 --> 00:00:59,247
events, planning and parallel work.

17
00:01:00,307 --> 00:01:01,027
These are examples.

18
00:01:02,007 --> 00:01:04,727
Agreeing on the outward promises gives each

19
00:01:04,887 --> 00:01:07,147
builder freedom to improve what happens inside.

20
00:01:09,714 --> 00:01:13,534
The same building blocks also support improving the system itself.

21
00:01:14,294 --> 00:01:17,234
An improvement team can work alongside everyone else.

22
00:01:18,234 --> 00:01:21,554
Working agents ask for technical help and unblockers;

23
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:24,234
the improvement team coaches and guides them.

24
00:01:25,154 --> 00:01:27,714
It can also make code and system changes across

25
00:01:27,714 --> 00:01:32,374
experiences, conversations, connections, agents and tools.

26
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:37,364
Or that team can work in a separate environment,

27
00:01:37,814 --> 00:01:39,734
with its own conversation people can join.

28
00:01:40,574 --> 00:01:44,994
It studies evidence, tests ideas and brings changes back through

29
00:01:44,994 --> 00:01:48,814
supported interfaces—even when the working environment needs repair.

30
00:01:49,934 --> 00:01:52,214
Either arrangement can improve every level.

31
00:01:52,934 --> 00:01:55,214
Their location and usual approach differ.

32
00:01:56,274 --> 00:02:02,154
That is the opportunity: dependable connections, reusable capabilities, and room for

33
00:02:02,334 --> 00:02:06,134
people and agents to build something we have not imagined yet.
